---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"
import SvgDefs from "../components/SvgDefs.astro"
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro"
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro"
import Message from "../components/Message.astro"
import MemoSaved from "../components/MemoSaved.astro"
import WaitlistBand from "../components/WaitlistBand.astro"

const schema = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "AboutPage",
    name: "About Threa",
    url: new URL("/about", Astro.site).href,
    mainEntity: {
      "@type": "Person",
      name: "Kristoffer Remback",
      sameAs: ["https://github.com/kristofferremback", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/kristofferremback/"],
    },
  },
]
---

<Layout
  title="About · Threa"
  description="Threa began as a side project, out of curiosity and frustration with workplace chat: how much more you can do with what a conversation already holds, and whether a tool like this has to lock you in. Built by Kristoffer Remback, in the open."
  schema={schema}
>
  <SvgDefs />
  <SiteHeader current="about" />

  <main id="main" class="about">
    <section class="section ab-hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="wrap ab-grid">
        <h1 id="hero-title" class="h1">Threa came out of curiosity and frustration.</h1>
        <p class="lede ab-lead">
          Hi, I'm Kristoffer. I'm building Threa. My day job is software
          engineering, where I spend a lot of time in tools that are fine but
          never great. The little frustrations add up, and eventually my
          curiosity got out of hand. So now there's this.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-band ab-strands" aria-labelledby="strands-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="ab-grid ab-intro">
          <h2 id="strands-title" class="h2">What I kept running into.</h2>
          <p class="lede">Three of them stuck around long enough that I did something about them.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="ab-grid ab-strand">
          <div class="ab-copy">
            <h3 class="h3">What did we say again?</h3>
            <p class="body">
              Years of decisions and their reasoning pile up in workplace chat,
              and I rarely find them again. My memory runs on gist: I'll remember
              that we discussed something, sometimes why, rarely the exact wording
              or where we said it, though I'll know it was Kate who said it. I
              started wondering whether a chat app could do something more useful
              with all that conversational data, keeping decisions and their
              reasoning tied to the messages they came from. I assumed it would
              cost too much. So far it hasn't.
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure class="app-ui ab-scene ab-scene-kept" aria-hidden="true">
            <p class="ab-meta"><span>#launch</span><span>Oct 30</span></p>
            <Message author="alex" time="14:05">
              <div class="tl-text">the embargo note says the 21st, not the 14th</div>
            </Message>
            <Message author="maya" time="14:06">
              <div class="tl-text">then launch moves to the 21st. I'll tell press</div>
            </Message>
            <MemoSaved title="Launch moved to the 21st to line up with the press embargo" />
          </figure>
        </div>

        <div class="ab-grid ab-strand is-flipped">
          <div class="ab-copy">
            <h3 class="h3">Tools are supposed to be yours.</h3>
            <p class="body">
              Most tools want to become the platform you can't afford to leave, and
              lately plenty of them insist on shipping their own AI agent. I rarely
              want it. The agent I already use has my codebase, my tools, and the
              context I've built around it. Another agent inside another app starts
              without them. Threa has Ariadne too, and I want her to be genuinely
              great, but she's at her best inside the room, where the shared context
              lives. For my own work I'd rather bring the agent I already use, so
              Threa connects to it instead of trying to replace it.
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure class="app-ui ab-scene" aria-hidden="true">
            <p class="ab-meta"><span>#api-v3</span><span>Apr 20</span></p>
            <Message author="alex" time="16:20">
              <div class="tl-text"><span class="mention is-bot">@claude-code</span> does the rotation fix cover mobile sessions too?</div>
            </Message>
            <Message author="claude-code" time="16:21">
              <div class="tl-text">Not yet. The migration in rotation.ts only moves web refresh tokens. I've started on mobile in <span class="ref-pill">auth-rotation</span>.</div>
            </Message>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <div class="ab-grid ab-strand">
          <div class="ab-copy">
            <h3 class="h3">Chat could be so much nicer.</h3>
            <p class="body">
              Nested threads, quoting, replying to one message in a busy room,
              formatting that behaves. None of it sells a platform, which is
              probably why it keeps getting skipped, but it all adds up over a day
              spent in chat. After years of putting up with the basics done badly,
              I think we deserve nice things.
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure class="app-ui ab-scene" aria-hidden="true">
            <p class="ab-meta"><span>#product</span><span>May 7</span></p>
            <Message author="jordan" time="10:02" class="is-noise">
              <div class="tl-text">standup moved to 10:30 btw</div>
            </Message>
            <Message author="sam" time="10:03" class="is-noise">
              <div class="tl-text">pizza again on friday? taking orders</div>
            </Message>
            <Message author="maya" time="10:04">
              <div class="quote-card">
                <div class="qm"><svg><use href="#quote-icon" /></svg></div>
                <div class="q-author">
                  <div class="q-avatar tl-avatar av-sam">SP</div>
                  <div class="q-name">Sam Patel</div>
                  <div class="q-time">09:41</div>
                </div>
                <div class="q-body">empty states for the board are on staging now</div>
              </div>
              <div class="tl-text">These look great. Can they ship with v3 on Thursday?</div>
              <div class="reactions"><span class="rxn"><span class="em">🙌</span><span class="num">2</span></span></div>
            </Message>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="team-title">
      <div class="wrap ab-grid ab-team">
        <div class="ab-letter">
          <h2 id="team-title" class="h2">I'm the team.</h2>
          <p>
            Hi, I'm Kristoffer. I've been paid to build software for the last
            decade. During parental leave I started tinkering on Threa to keep
            myself from going insane. Not sure it worked: it's late, and I'm
            telling my computer why I'm building this.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ab-sig">
          <p class="ab-sig-who">
            <span class="ab-sig-mark" aria-hidden="true">KR</span>
            <span class="ab-sig-name">Kristoffer Remback</span>
          </p>
          <ul class="ab-links">
            <li><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/kristofferremback" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">GitHub</a></li>
            <li><a class="text-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kristofferremback/" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
      <div class="wrap ab-grid ab-principles">
        <h2 id="principles-title" class="h2">Built the way I want tools to work.</h2>
        <p class="ab-stance">
          Good at its job, composable with everything else, and easy to step away
          from. Threa is built that way on purpose. The door stays open, so if you
          stay it's because you want to, not because leaving would cost you.
        </p>
        <div class="ab-practice">
          <p class="lede">
            It has also been my way into building with AI agents. Most of Threa is
            written by directing them, but the thinking stays mine, and that matters
            more than ever. They're a good way to chase a curiosity, and you can get
            decent software out of them as long as you do the thinking
            yourself. Seeing where they shine and where they fall short has been half
            the fun. It's a work in progress, on what I think is a good trajectory.
          </p>
          <ul class="ab-links">
            <li><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/threahq/threa">Browse the source on GitHub</a></li>
            <li><a class="text-link" href="/developers/feature-requests">Request a feature</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <WaitlistBand
      source="about"
      lede="Threa is early, and there's plenty left to build. Join the waitlist, or follow along in the public repo."
    />
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />

  <script is:inline>
    /* The page's one moment: when the first scene scrolls into view, the two
       source messages glow and the memory line lands under them, the way the app
       marks a capture. Without the observer, or with reduced motion, the scene
       is simply shown finished. */
    (function () {
      const scene = document.querySelector(".ab-scene-kept")
      if (!scene || !("IntersectionObserver" in window)) return
      if (matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches) return
      scene.classList.add("is-waiting")
      const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
        if (!entries.some((e) => e.intersectionRatio >= 0.8)) return
        io.disconnect()
        scene.classList.add("is-kept")
      }, { threshold: 0.8 })
      io.observe(scene)
    })()
  </script>

  <style>
    /* The page keeps the site's 12-column axes, but each section changes
       shape around them: a headline across the full width, strands that swap
       sides with a strip of the app sliding in from the page edge, a note
       signed in the margin. */
    .ab-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(12, minmax(0, 1fr));
      column-gap: 32px;
    }

    .ab-hero .h1 {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
      margin-bottom: 44px;
      font-size: clamp(44px, 6.6vw, 96px);
      letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    }
    .ab-lead {
      grid-column: 7 / -1;
      font-size: 20px;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: hsl(var(--ink));
    }

    .ab-intro {
      align-items: baseline;
    }
    .ab-intro .h2 {
      grid-column: 1 / span 5;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .ab-intro .lede {
      grid-column: 7 / -1;
    }

    .ab-strands {
      overflow-x: clip;
    }
    .ab-strand {
      margin-top: clamp(72px, 9vw, 120px);
      align-items: center;
    }
    .ab-intro + .ab-strand {
      margin-top: clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px);
    }
    .ab-copy {
      grid-column: 1 / span 6;
      grid-row: 1;
    }
    .ab-scene {
      grid-column: 8 / -1;
      grid-row: 1;
    }
    .ab-strand.is-flipped .ab-copy {
      grid-column: 7 / -1;
    }
    .ab-strand.is-flipped .ab-scene {
      grid-column: 1 / span 5;
    }
    .ab-copy .h3 {
      margin-bottom: 14px;
      font-size: clamp(24px, 2.5vw, 32px);
    }
    .ab-copy .body {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 17px;
    }

    /* A paper strip that bleeds off the side it sits on. */
    .ab-scene {
      position: relative;
      isolation: isolate;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 18px 0 22px;
    }
    .ab-scene::before {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      z-index: -1;
      inset: 0 -100vw 0 -24px;
      background: hsl(var(--paper));
      border: 1px solid hsl(var(--line));
      border-right: 0;
      border-radius: 16px 0 0 16px;
    }
    .ab-strand.is-flipped .ab-scene::before {
      inset: 0 -24px 0 -100vw;
      border: 1px solid hsl(var(--line));
      border-left: 0;
      border-radius: 0 16px 16px 0;
    }
    .ab-meta {
      display: flex;
      gap: 10px;
      margin: 0 0 4px;
      padding: 0 16px;
      font-size: 13px;
      color: hsl(var(--muted));
    }
    .ab-meta span:first-child {
      font-weight: 500;
      color: hsl(var(--ink));
    }

    /* The team section reads as a note: the heading runs into the paragraph
       at reading size, signed off in the margin. */
    .ab-team {
      align-items: end;
    }
    .ab-letter {
      grid-column: 1 / span 8;
    }
    .ab-letter .h2,
    .ab-letter p {
      display: inline;
      font-size: clamp(22px, 2.3vw, 30px);
      line-height: 1.45;
    }
    .ab-letter .h2 {
      margin: 0 0.15em 0 0;
      letter-spacing: -0.012em;
    }
    .ab-letter p {
      margin: 0;
      color: hsl(var(--ink-soft));
    }
    .ab-sig {
      grid-column: 10 / -1;
    }
    .ab-sig-who {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 12px;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .ab-sig-mark {
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      flex: none;
      width: 44px;
      height: 44px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      background: hsl(var(--gold) / 0.16);
      color: hsl(var(--ink));
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-weight: var(--display-weight);
      font-size: 16px;
    }
    .ab-sig-name {
      font-size: 16px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: hsl(var(--ink));
    }
    .ab-links {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0 28px;
      margin: 16px 0 0;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;
    }

    .ab-principles {
      align-items: start;
    }
    .ab-principles .h2 {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
      margin-bottom: clamp(32px, 4vw, 56px);
      font-size: clamp(36px, 4.6vw, 64px);
      letter-spacing: -0.028em;
      line-height: 1.02;
    }
    .ab-stance {
      grid-column: 1 / span 5;
      margin: 0;
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-weight: 500;
      font-size: clamp(20px, 1.9vw, 24px);
      line-height: 1.35;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      color: hsl(var(--ink));
      text-wrap: pretty;
    }
    .ab-practice {
      grid-column: 7 / -1;
      padding-top: 4px;
    }

    .ab-scene-kept.is-waiting :global(.memo-saved) {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(6px);
    }
    .ab-scene-kept.is-kept :global(.memo-saved) {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
      transition: opacity 0.5s ease-out 1.1s, transform 0.5s ease-out 1.1s;
    }
    .ab-scene-kept.is-kept :global(.tl-row) {
      animation: kept-glow 2.4s ease-in-out 0.2s both;
    }
    @keyframes kept-glow {
      0%, 100% { background-color: hsl(var(--gold) / 0); }
      30%, 55% { background-color: hsl(var(--gold) / 0.12); }
    }

    @media (max-width: 880px) {
      .ab-grid {
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      }
      .ab-grid > *,
      .ab-intro .h2,
      .ab-intro .lede,
      .ab-strand.is-flipped .ab-copy,
      .ab-strand.is-flipped .ab-scene {
        grid-column: 1;
        grid-row: auto;
      }
      .ab-hero .h1 {
        margin-bottom: 24px;
      }
      .ab-lead {
        font-size: 18px;
      }
      .ab-intro .h2 {
        margin-bottom: 16px;
      }
      .ab-strand {
        margin-top: 64px;
      }
      .ab-intro + .ab-strand {
        margin-top: 48px;
      }
      .ab-scene {
        margin-top: 28px;
      }
      .ab-scene::before,
      .ab-strand.is-flipped .ab-scene::before {
        inset: 0 -100vw;
        border-left: 0;
        border-right: 0;
        border-radius: 0;
      }
      .ab-copy .h3 {
        margin-bottom: 10px;
      }
      .ab-copy .body {
        font-size: 16px;
      }
      .ab-sig {
        margin-top: 36px;
      }
      .ab-practice {
        margin-top: 28px;
        padding-top: 0;
      }
    }

    @media (max-width: 560px) {
      .ab-meta {
        padding: 0;
      }
      .ab-scene :global(.tl-row) {
        padding-left: 0;
        padding-right: 0;
      }
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
